The film grain overlay is installed and wired into `index.html`, but I couldn't render a frame to check it visually: there is no Chrome on this machine and the download was blocked.

- **Installed:** the registry's `grain-overlay` component, at `compositions/components/grain-overlay.html`.
- **Wired:** the overlay markup is the last child of `#main`, and its CSS sits in a new `<style>` block in the head. It covers the full frame above the title and caption for the whole 10 seconds.
- **Lint:** `hyperframes lint` reports one error and one warning, both about `#main` having no `window.__timelines` registration. The file had no script before my change, so I left that alone. The warning's suggested fix is adding `data-no-timeline` to `#main`, which also avoids a 45-second wait on every render.

Grain strength is the `opacity: 0.15` on `.grain-texture`, and flicker speed is the `0.5s` animation duration, if you want it heavier or subtler.

The registry configured in `hyperframes.json` (`https://localhost:4890/registry`) failed to serve almost every item during search, so the search returned nothing. The direct `hyperframes add grain-overlay` still succeeded.

