answer:
The film grain overlay is in the composition, but I couldn't render a frame to confirm it visually: there's no Chrome in this environment and the download was blocked.

I installed the registry's `grain-overlay` component with `hyperframes add grain-overlay` and pasted its snippet into `index.html` as the last child of `#main`. It is a full-frame animated noise texture at 15% opacity that sits above the title and caption for the whole 10 seconds.

`hyperframes lint` reports one error and one warning. Both are about the composition having no `window.__timelines` registration, which comes from the original file rather than the overlay. I left that alone; the linter says adding `data-no-timeline` to `#main` avoids a 45-second wait on every render.

To tune the look, edit the `.grain-texture` rule in `index.html`: `opacity` (0.15) controls strength and the animation duration (0.5s) controls flicker speed.

The install also added `compositions/components/grain-overlay.html` (the reference copy of the snippet) and `hyperframes.lock.json`, plus CLI state under `.hyperframes/` and `.cache/`.

